--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-coupon-base-and-expiry/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Why
+
+Two behaviours contradict the README business rules: a percentage coupon is computed on the gross amount instead of the subtotal after volume discounts (finance: 12 notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon give €48.00 instead of €48.60), and a coupon is refused on its last valid day (customer: AUTUMN refused on 30 November).
+
+## What Changes
+
+- A percentage coupon is applied to the order subtotal after volume discounts.
+- A coupon is accepted on its last day (`validUntil` is inclusive).
+- Not changed: VAT on shipping. A customer asked to remove it, but the README says shipping is subject to 22% VAT; that needs a business decision and is left for a separate request.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `discounts`: volume discounts and coupons, their base and validity period.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/pricing.ts`, `src/coupons.ts`, plus tests.
